WEBVTT

1
00:01:24.376 --> 00:01:25.711
Your Grace.

2
00:02:09.254 --> 00:02:12.549
Sergeant, I'm here on behalf
of the Red Cross

3
00:02:12.633 --> 00:02:14.393
and I'd like to speak
with General Kitchener.

4
00:02:14.426 --> 00:02:16.303
There is no General Kitchener here.

5
00:02:16.386 --> 00:02:18.805
Your Grace? Your Grace?
Let... Let him in.

6
00:02:20.682 --> 00:02:22.660
Well, if Morton's here,
then Kitchener can't be far away.

7
00:02:22.684 --> 00:02:24.645
My apologies, Your Grace.

8
00:02:24.728 --> 00:02:26.146
Security's paramount right now.

9
00:02:26.229 --> 00:02:28.398
It's a secret that you're
visiting with the general.

10
00:02:28.482 --> 00:02:30.275
We can't be too careful
with these Boers

11
00:02:30.359 --> 00:02:31.693
and their guerrilla tactics.

12
00:02:31.777 --> 00:02:32.861
Too careful?

13
00:02:32.944 --> 00:02:35.572
Looks like this place
could use a lot more care.

14
00:02:35.656 --> 00:02:38.116
Begging your pardon, sir,
but these concentration camps

15
00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.427
are the reason we're winning this war.

16
00:02:39.451 --> 00:02:40.744
This way.

17
00:02:44.956 --> 00:02:49.378
Orlando. Our knight in shining armor.

18
00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:51.338
Thank you for coming.

19
00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.340
What's going on, Kitchener?

20
00:02:54.091 --> 00:02:55.676
It seems that you've been

21
00:02:55.759 --> 00:02:57.028
somewhat liberal with the truth.

22
00:02:57.052 --> 00:02:59.346
Time has not been kind here.

23
00:02:59.429 --> 00:03:01.109
Well, you'll have to explain that
to Emily.

24
00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:04.017
On my return to England,
it will be my first port of call.

25
00:03:04.101 --> 00:03:05.185
She's outside,

26
00:03:05.268 --> 00:03:07.062
with Conrad.

27
00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:09.898
Why are we here, Mother?

28
00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:13.443
Do you remember why
King Arthur and his knights

29
00:03:13.527 --> 00:03:14.903
had a round table?

30
00:03:16.988 --> 00:03:19.116
Because it meant
that all men were equal.

31
00:03:20.075 --> 00:03:22.369
It's important that people
born into privilege

32
00:03:22.452 --> 00:03:23.787
lead by example.

33
00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:27.124
That's why your father and I
are patrons of the Red Cross.

34
00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:29.418
Helping others,

35
00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:32.337
not hiding behind our status.

36
00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:38.844
Never forget that.

37
00:03:39.428 --> 00:03:40.887
Hmm?

38
00:03:43.557 --> 00:03:45.684
I'm just going to check on your father.

39
00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:50.480
Stay here, Conrad.

40
00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:58.488
This terrible war would be over, Shola,

41
00:03:59.197 --> 00:04:02.784
if King Arthur and his
noble knights were still here.

42
00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:06.371
Of course.
And which one would you be?

43
00:04:06.455 --> 00:04:09.040
I'd be Lancelot.

44
00:04:09.124 --> 00:04:11.835
Father would be Arthur.
Mother, Guinevere.

45
00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:15.005
And you, the mighty Merlin.

46
00:04:15.088 --> 00:04:16.089
Really?

47
00:04:17.466 --> 00:04:20.677
This is ridiculous.
We're wasting precious time.

48
00:04:20.761 --> 00:04:22.888
Look around, people are dying.

49
00:04:22.971 --> 00:04:25.015
We have emergency supplies
from the Red Cross.

50
00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:26.767
Thank God she's on our side.

51
00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:28.185
Well, on my side, at least.

52
00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:29.478
She's more of a force

53
00:04:29.561 --> 00:04:30.771
than any of our enemies.

54
00:04:30.854 --> 00:04:32.314
There's General Kitchener.

55
00:04:32.397 --> 00:04:35.734
Well, open the gates!
Bring in those supplies!

56
00:04:35.817 --> 00:04:37.360
Emily!

57
00:04:44.034 --> 00:04:45.619
Lie down until I get back.

58
00:04:58.298 --> 00:04:59.298
Go back to Conrad.

59
00:05:05.889 --> 00:05:07.432
Go to hell, Kitchener.

60
00:05:12.521 --> 00:05:15.315
I got him! Stop fire!

61
00:05:19.736 --> 00:05:22.280
Emily!

62
00:05:22.948 --> 00:05:25.075
Cease fire!

63
00:05:28.954 --> 00:05:29.955
Emily.

64
00:05:31.081 --> 00:05:32.958
Darling, I'm here.

65
00:05:36.378 --> 00:05:39.172
I'm here. Darling, I'm here.

66
00:05:40.757 --> 00:05:42.968
That's it. I'm here.
You have to stay with me.

67
00:05:43.802 --> 00:05:45.262
You have to stay with me.

68
00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:46.555
Darling?

69
00:05:49.099 --> 00:05:51.017
Protect our son.

70
00:05:52.894 --> 00:05:56.565
Protect him from this world. And...

71
00:05:57.691 --> 00:06:00.026
Never let him see war again.

72
00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.994
Promise me.

73
00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:11.872
I promise.

74
00:07:51.638 --> 00:07:53.264
- You know, Conrad...
- Hmm?

75
00:07:53.348 --> 00:07:56.267
Up there, I feel free.

76
00:07:56.351 --> 00:07:59.980
Yes, I'm very much looking forward
to my first solo flight.

77
00:08:00.063 --> 00:08:02.148
Remember what happened
to Icarus, Conrad,

78
00:08:02.232 --> 00:08:04.484
when he flew too close to the sun.

79
00:08:05.193 --> 00:08:07.862
Well, I remember him
needing to escape, no?

80
00:08:07.946 --> 00:08:09.990
Well, he got burned.

81
00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:12.826
I think we both see
that story differently.

82
00:08:12.909 --> 00:08:14.953
- Welcome home, Your Grace.
- Thank you, Shola.

83
00:08:16.246 --> 00:08:19.332
- Afternoon, everyone.
Afternoon, Your Grace.

84
00:08:20.083 --> 00:08:21.683
Ready for your maiden flight yet, Shola?

85
00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:23.795
Well, if God wanted man to fly,

86
00:08:23.878 --> 00:08:25.130
he would have given him wings.

87
00:08:25.213 --> 00:08:28.216
Yes, I suppose.
You drive Father's car?

88
00:08:28.299 --> 00:08:29.634
Mmm-hmm.

89
00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:31.803
You haven't any wheels.

90
00:08:44.274 --> 00:08:45.274
Nanny Watkins.

91
00:08:47.861 --> 00:08:49.571
My study in five minutes.

92
00:08:53.033 --> 00:08:54.534
Your Grace.

93
00:09:05.378 --> 00:09:06.504
Your Grace.

94
00:09:06.588 --> 00:09:09.424
I should be reprimanding you
for your insolence.

95
00:09:10.216 --> 00:09:12.552
Your opinion behind closed doors
is one thing, Polly,

96
00:09:12.635 --> 00:09:14.846
but I will not tolerate
such demonstrations

97
00:09:14.929 --> 00:09:16.056
in front of my household.

98
00:09:16.681 --> 00:09:19.809
I'll play by your rules
when you play by mine.

99
00:09:19.893 --> 00:09:22.062
Do you really think
you can keep secrets from me?

100
00:09:22.687 --> 00:09:23.772
What do you mean?

101
00:09:23.855 --> 00:09:26.816
Once again, you've turned down
Cousin Felix's invitation

102
00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:28.777
for Conrad to stay with him in Russia.

103
00:09:29.652 --> 00:09:30.820
And how do you know that?

104
00:09:31.488 --> 00:09:33.573
Us nannies love a good gossip.

105
00:09:33.656 --> 00:09:34.949
And we've all noticed

106
00:09:35.033 --> 00:09:37.535
that you've no problem
with Felix traveling here,

107
00:09:37.619 --> 00:09:40.330
but you seem to have a problem
with Conrad traveling there.

108
00:09:40.413 --> 00:09:41.998
Or anywhere, for that matter.

109
00:09:42.749 --> 00:09:46.377
Yeah. Guilty as charged.
Well, I'm sorry.

110
00:09:46.461 --> 00:09:48.171
I should have discussed it with you.

111
00:09:48.671 --> 00:09:50.799
Has all this flying around in circles

112
00:09:50.882 --> 00:09:51.942
made you forget your manners?

113
00:09:51.966 --> 00:09:53.593
Well, what have I done now?

114
00:09:53.676 --> 00:09:55.220
You haven't even offered me a drink.

115
00:09:55.303 --> 00:09:57.263
Oh, yes, I'm sorry.

116
00:09:58.431 --> 00:10:00.642
And if we had discussed this,

117
00:10:00.725 --> 00:10:02.769
what would my opinion have been?

118
00:10:03.478 --> 00:10:05.647
You think that my

119
00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:08.900
fear for Conrad's safety is a weakness.

120
00:10:08.983 --> 00:10:10.527
Fear is natural.

121
00:10:11.277 --> 00:10:13.154
The problem is,
the more you fear something,

122
00:10:13.238 --> 00:10:15.031
the more likely it is to come true.

123
00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:19.953
Hmm. So, then,
we're both in need of a nanny.

124
00:10:20.036 --> 00:10:22.330
So it would seem.

125
00:10:36.344 --> 00:10:37.679
Higher!

126
00:10:45.603 --> 00:10:47.564
Can you fight with only one arm?

127
00:10:47.647 --> 00:10:49.274
Oh, yes.

128
00:10:49.858 --> 00:10:51.776
If I had someone left to fight.

129
00:10:57.407 --> 00:11:00.326
Shola. Do you really think
a knife can beat a bullet?

130
00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:03.288
This is how people
are fighting nowadays.

131
00:11:03.371 --> 00:11:04.664
Now, clean yourselves up

132
00:11:04.747 --> 00:11:07.208
before this afternoon's appointment.

133
00:11:23.766 --> 00:11:26.769
My father also brought me here
for my first suit.

134
00:11:27.353 --> 00:11:30.356
Kingsman, world's finest tailor.

135
00:11:38.072 --> 00:11:40.200
- Morning.
- Your Grace.

136
00:11:40.283 --> 00:11:42.243
Fitting room number one
is ready for you.

137
00:11:42.327 --> 00:11:43.995
Thank you.

138
00:11:46.497 --> 00:11:48.291
Well, here we are.

139
00:11:49.918 --> 00:11:51.961
I wish your mother could see you now.

140
00:11:52.503 --> 00:11:54.589
She would've been so proud.

141
00:11:55.715 --> 00:11:57.425
I hope so, Father.

142
00:11:59.719 --> 00:12:03.598
Although, I might get more use
out of a shooting suit or

143
00:12:03.681 --> 00:12:06.142
a smoking jacket, you know.

144
00:12:06.226 --> 00:12:09.479
Whatever might help
in the pursuit of fine birds.

145
00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:12.065
Oh, come on, Father.

146
00:12:12.899 --> 00:12:14.317
It's a big world out there.

147
00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:15.401
Sooner or later,

148
00:12:15.485 --> 00:12:17.405
you're going to have to
let me enjoy it, even if,

149
00:12:18.321 --> 00:12:19.864
you know, even if you don't want to.

150
00:12:22.367 --> 00:12:23.534
You know,

151
00:12:23.618 --> 00:12:24.827
Conrad,

152
00:12:27.247 --> 00:12:30.416
our ancestors,
they were terrible people.

153
00:12:30.959 --> 00:12:34.754
They robbed, lied, pillaged,
and killed, until one day,

154
00:12:34.837 --> 00:12:37.215
they found themselves noblemen.

155
00:12:38.049 --> 00:12:39.676
But that nobility,

156
00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:42.845
it never came from chivalry.

157
00:12:43.763 --> 00:12:46.557
It came from being tough and ruthless.

158
00:12:47.475 --> 00:12:51.562
Back then, to be called a "gentleman"

159
00:12:51.646 --> 00:12:53.523
would have been a death sentence.

160
00:12:54.399 --> 00:12:59.320
Not the mark of honor it is today.

161
00:12:59.904 --> 00:13:01.489
We are Oxfords,

162
00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:04.200
not rogues.

163
00:13:06.953 --> 00:13:07.954
Oxford!

164
00:13:08.037 --> 00:13:10.665
- Kitchener.

165
00:13:10.748 --> 00:13:12.542
Well, so glad we share the same tailor.

166
00:13:12.625 --> 00:13:15.962
Indeed. Well, the Kingsman clientele
is enough to make any club envious.

167
00:13:16.045 --> 00:13:19.090
Mmm-hmm. Oxford, can I
borrow you for a moment?

168
00:13:19.590 --> 00:13:20.717
Is there somewhere private?

169
00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:22.677
May I suggest the pattern room
upstairs, sir.

170
00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:24.053
Perfect.

171
00:13:24.137 --> 00:13:27.056
Conrad, this is Morton,
my aide-de-camp.

172
00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:29.559
Morton, look after
young Conrad for us, will you?

173
00:13:29.642 --> 00:13:31.060
It will be my pleasure, my lord.

174
00:13:31.144 --> 00:13:32.145
Good.

175
00:13:42.655 --> 00:13:45.450
I gather you turned down
our Austrian friend

176
00:13:45.533 --> 00:13:48.619
Archduke Ferdinand's
invitation to his shoot.

177
00:13:49.454 --> 00:13:51.539
Surely your pacifism doesn't extend

178
00:13:51.622 --> 00:13:53.541
to a few birds, does it?

179
00:13:53.624 --> 00:13:55.251
Us bumping into each other here

180
00:13:55.335 --> 00:13:57.295
was no coincidence, was it?

181
00:13:58.629 --> 00:14:01.174
Walls have ears
in Whitehall these days.

182
00:14:01.674 --> 00:14:05.136
Which is why I felt Kingsman
a safer place for a chat.

183
00:14:05.219 --> 00:14:06.596
Mmm-hmm.

184
00:14:06.679 --> 00:14:09.307
I'm worried that Ferdinand's
political ambitions

185
00:14:09.390 --> 00:14:11.100
may be putting him in danger.

186
00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:15.146
I need you to do me a small favor.

187
00:14:15.229 --> 00:14:17.231
What sort of favor?

188
00:14:17.315 --> 00:14:18.876
So, you're serious
about being a soldier?

189
00:14:18.900 --> 00:14:20.902
- Oh, yes.
- Which regiment?

190
00:14:20.985 --> 00:14:22.111
Uh... Grenadiers.

191
00:14:22.195 --> 00:14:23.613
Grenadiers. Well,

192
00:14:23.696 --> 00:14:26.240
when the time comes, contact me.

193
00:14:26.324 --> 00:14:27.367
I'll see what I can do.

194
00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:28.785
Conrad.

195
00:14:31.579 --> 00:14:34.082
You're going to need
that shooting suit after all.

196
00:15:19.502 --> 00:15:21.212
My Shepherd.

197
00:15:21.295 --> 00:15:25.633
I have a Fabergé egg
made especially for you.

198
00:15:25.716 --> 00:15:27.510
And look inside.

199
00:15:28.719 --> 00:15:31.431
A little replica of Angus,

200
00:15:31.514 --> 00:15:33.307
your favorite goat.

201
00:15:33.391 --> 00:15:34.725
You're late.

202
00:15:35.643 --> 00:15:37.311
Take a seat.

203
00:15:39.355 --> 00:15:42.900
What is trust? Hmm?

204
00:15:44.026 --> 00:15:47.321
Trust is having confidence

205
00:15:47.405 --> 00:15:49.282
in the honesty of another.

206
00:15:50.324 --> 00:15:52.952
That will be our weapon

207
00:15:53.035 --> 00:15:56.038
to change the world.

208
00:15:56.122 --> 00:15:58.374
Who do I trust?

209
00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:01.377
Animals.

210
00:16:01.461 --> 00:16:04.255
They never let me down

211
00:16:04.338 --> 00:16:08.342
and they follow my commands blindly.

212
00:16:08.885 --> 00:16:11.345
The question I now have is

213
00:16:11.429 --> 00:16:16.017
can I trust you to behave like them?

214
00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:18.352
Open the boxes in front of you.

215
00:16:22.148 --> 00:16:26.944
These rings will be the symbol
of membership to my flock.

216
00:16:27.028 --> 00:16:31.407
Put them on, and you will
share in our successes.

217
00:16:31.491 --> 00:16:32.533
But,

218
00:16:33.201 --> 00:16:34.535
break my trust,

219
00:16:34.619 --> 00:16:37.288
and inside you will find

220
00:16:37.914 --> 00:16:40.458
my final gift to you.

221
00:16:40.541 --> 00:16:42.126
A tortoise?

222
00:16:42.210 --> 00:16:45.463
Am I not worthy of a better animal?

223
00:16:45.546 --> 00:16:48.508
Rasputin, I have a bear.
I will happily exchange it with you.

224
00:16:48.591 --> 00:16:51.969
Yes, Princip.
I will be the great bear of Russia.

225
00:16:52.053 --> 00:16:53.679
Take what you believe is yours.

226
00:16:54.263 --> 00:16:56.015
And by all means,

227
00:16:56.098 --> 00:16:58.059
treat our Shepherd
with the same respect you hold

228
00:16:58.142 --> 00:17:01.020
for that joke of a man
who calls himself your tsar.

229
00:17:01.103 --> 00:17:04.148
Go ahead, Rasputin, take it.

230
00:17:04.649 --> 00:17:06.526
- I dare you.

231
00:17:06.609 --> 00:17:07.902
Now, now, Mata and Erik.

232
00:17:07.985 --> 00:17:10.154
We are a team.

233
00:17:10.238 --> 00:17:13.074
And Rasputin here...

234
00:17:13.866 --> 00:17:17.703
is like my beloved Angus.

235
00:17:18.913 --> 00:17:21.082
Always butting

236
00:17:22.333 --> 00:17:23.918
and fucking.

237
00:17:28.130 --> 00:17:31.592
But do not mistake fondness
for weakness,

238
00:17:31.676 --> 00:17:34.345
you late Russian fuckstick!

239
00:17:36.013 --> 00:17:37.974
As everybody knows,

240
00:17:38.891 --> 00:17:40.518
the tortoise

241
00:17:41.811 --> 00:17:44.230
eventually wins the race.

242
00:17:52.446 --> 00:17:53.573
Now...

243
00:17:56.158 --> 00:18:00.663
my spy, or should I say my mole,

244
00:18:00.746 --> 00:18:03.457
in the British government

245
00:18:03.541 --> 00:18:08.004
informs me that Kitchener is
concerned for the safety

246
00:18:08.087 --> 00:18:10.089
of the Archduke Ferdinand.

247
00:18:10.965 --> 00:18:14.594
Princip, my wee bear.

248
00:18:14.677 --> 00:18:16.429
Are you ready to prove

249
00:18:16.512 --> 00:18:19.265
Kitchener's concerns are justified?

250
00:18:19.348 --> 00:18:22.184
Yes, I am, my Shepherd.
And I will not let you down.

251
00:18:22.685 --> 00:18:25.021
Damn fucking right.

252
00:19:03.726 --> 00:19:06.062
Does that make sense
to you, Ferdinand?

253
00:19:06.145 --> 00:19:08.272
Ah, now I understand

254
00:19:08.356 --> 00:19:11.067
why you accepted my shooting invitation.

255
00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:15.237
I didn't really believe
Kitchener's scare tactics.

256
00:19:15.321 --> 00:19:17.948
Harping on about my being in danger.

257
00:19:18.032 --> 00:19:20.785
Well, only a fool ignores
a friend's warning, Ferdi.

258
00:19:20.868 --> 00:19:22.328
Is it really too much to ask?

259
00:19:22.411 --> 00:19:25.122
I think you should come back with me
and hear what he has to say.

260
00:19:25.206 --> 00:19:28.501
Turning you down is a hard task.

261
00:19:28.584 --> 00:19:30.920
I will give you my decision tonight.

262
00:19:31.003 --> 00:19:32.004
Good.

263
00:19:51.774 --> 00:19:55.277
- Drive! Drive!

264
00:20:08.207 --> 00:20:10.584
I come here on a visit of goodwill,

265
00:20:10.668 --> 00:20:12.086
to be greeted by bombs?

266
00:20:14.296 --> 00:20:15.339
Yes.

267
00:20:15.423 --> 00:20:17.842
It gives me special pleasure...

268
00:20:17.925 --> 00:20:20.010
I... I shouldn't have brought you here.

269
00:20:20.094 --> 00:20:23.472
We need to get home,
where I can protect you.

270
00:20:23.556 --> 00:20:24.556
What...

271
00:20:24.974 --> 00:20:27.184
I just protected you.
I don't need protecting.

272
00:20:27.268 --> 00:20:30.187
Yes, you do, Conrad. I'm sorry,

273
00:20:30.271 --> 00:20:32.148
but you think you know
what the world is like,

274
00:20:32.231 --> 00:20:33.691
but the truth is, you're just a boy

275
00:20:33.774 --> 00:20:36.235
who has no idea
what men are capable of.

276
00:20:36.318 --> 00:20:39.113
What? Watching my mother die
wasn't a good enough introduction?

277
00:21:09.602 --> 00:21:10.895
Are you sure this is right?

278
00:21:10.978 --> 00:21:13.230
Just follow my orders.

279
00:21:14.023 --> 00:21:16.317
Take the first left.

280
00:21:29.538 --> 00:21:30.998
It's a dead end, you fool.

281
00:21:31.081 --> 00:21:32.625
I knew this was the wrong way.

282
00:21:32.708 --> 00:21:34.502
I meant the next left.

283
00:21:34.585 --> 00:21:36.253
Stop arguing.
We're sitting ducks here.

284
00:21:37.213 --> 00:21:38.464
Get this car moving now.

285
00:22:18.170 --> 00:22:20.840
Father, it's terrible
about Ferdi and Sophie.

286
00:22:22.883 --> 00:22:24.426
We're safe now, aren't we?

287
00:22:24.510 --> 00:22:26.804
Yes, but for how long?

288
00:22:26.887 --> 00:22:30.099
I'm beginning to understand
what Kitchener was so afraid of.

289
00:22:30.182 --> 00:22:31.392
Already there are rumors

290
00:22:31.475 --> 00:22:33.727
the Austrians are mobilizing their army.

291
00:22:33.811 --> 00:22:37.273
They don't believe this assassin
acted independently.

292
00:22:37.982 --> 00:22:39.650
And neither do I.

293
00:22:39.733 --> 00:22:40.776
It's just Serbia.

294
00:22:40.860 --> 00:22:42.580
I mean, it's such
a small part of the world.

295
00:22:42.611 --> 00:22:43.654
Why do they care?

296
00:22:44.238 --> 00:22:48.492
Well, because small things
can grow into big problems.

297
00:22:48.576 --> 00:22:50.619
You see, years ago,

298
00:22:50.703 --> 00:22:52.788
there were three young cousins.

299
00:22:52.872 --> 00:22:54.099
The eldest was a real troublemaker...

300
00:22:54.123 --> 00:22:55.332
Put my soldier back!

301
00:22:55.416 --> 00:22:56.750
There are no rules in war.

302
00:22:56.834 --> 00:22:59.086
- I'll teach you war, Wilhelm!

303
00:22:59.169 --> 00:23:00.754
Their grandmother
was Queen Victoria...

304
00:23:00.838 --> 00:23:02.047
Nicholas. Enough!

305
00:23:02.131 --> 00:23:03.340
Who kept them in line.

306
00:23:03.424 --> 00:23:07.052
They grew up to become
Kaiser Wilhelm of Germany,

307
00:23:07.136 --> 00:23:10.598
Tsar Nicholas of Russia,
and King George of England.

308
00:23:11.765 --> 00:23:13.642
And now,
poor Ferdinand's assassination

309
00:23:13.726 --> 00:23:15.769
has given the moronic kaiser

310
00:23:15.853 --> 00:23:19.356
a reason to reignite
their childhood feud.

311
00:23:21.442 --> 00:23:24.403
But surely they've matured
enough to avoid a war?

312
00:23:24.486 --> 00:23:26.280
One would hope so.

313
00:23:26.363 --> 00:23:29.158
And, thankfully,
we have our own King George

314
00:23:29.241 --> 00:23:31.201
to help keep the peace.

315
00:23:33.704 --> 00:23:35.664
Ah. There it is.

316
00:23:42.713 --> 00:23:44.048
Look at us.

317
00:23:45.591 --> 00:23:46.926
Three young cousins

318
00:23:47.009 --> 00:23:49.136
who thought they knew how to rule.

319
00:23:49.219 --> 00:23:51.430
But now the soldiers are real.

320
00:23:52.723 --> 00:23:54.475
Get two copies of this photograph made

321
00:23:54.558 --> 00:23:56.661
and have them delivered
with these letters immediately.

322
00:23:56.685 --> 00:23:58.520
I'll have Morton see to it personally.

323
00:23:58.604 --> 00:23:59.813
Excellent.

324
00:23:59.897 --> 00:24:01.440
Your Majesty.

325
00:24:07.071 --> 00:24:09.031
- Erik.
- My kaiser.

326
00:24:09.114 --> 00:24:13.077
"Restraint is a virtue.
Remember your duty."

327
00:24:13.827 --> 00:24:15.621
His Majesty, my cousin,
the king of England,

328
00:24:15.704 --> 00:24:18.332
strongly suggests we do nothing.

329
00:24:21.627 --> 00:24:24.838
Remember how Prince George
used to enjoy it

330
00:24:24.922 --> 00:24:26.131
when your English mother

331
00:24:26.215 --> 00:24:28.133
and her English doctors
would torture you?

332
00:24:28.217 --> 00:24:30.552
George would tease you about your...

333
00:24:32.179 --> 00:24:33.514
deformities.

334
00:24:34.390 --> 00:24:36.350
Yeah, yeah. Yeah.

335
00:24:36.433 --> 00:24:39.436
And don't forget
that sniggering at his side

336
00:24:39.520 --> 00:24:41.313
was your little Russian cousin,

337
00:24:42.314 --> 00:24:43.774
Tsar Nicholas.

338
00:24:43.857 --> 00:24:46.235
Cousin George
is imploring self-restraint

339
00:24:46.318 --> 00:24:49.196
against our other cousin,
the moronic kaiser.

340
00:24:49.697 --> 00:24:52.700
King George has always
protected our interests.

341
00:24:52.783 --> 00:24:55.452
Why would we go to war
over something so trivial?

342
00:24:55.536 --> 00:24:57.579
Because we gave Serbia our word.

343
00:24:57.663 --> 00:24:59.873
And besides, I hate the kaiser.

344
00:24:59.957 --> 00:25:01.792
It will be good for his oversized ego

345
00:25:01.875 --> 00:25:04.003
to match his undersized hand.

346
00:25:06.213 --> 00:25:08.632
A wise decision, my tsar.

347
00:25:09.174 --> 00:25:12.720
The soul of Russia is safe
in your hands.

348
00:25:14.596 --> 00:25:15.973
The world will laugh at you

349
00:25:16.056 --> 00:25:19.143
for not keeping your word
and standing by the Austrians.

350
00:25:20.394 --> 00:25:22.646
Ignore the English king.

351
00:25:23.981 --> 00:25:25.816
Tell George to mind
his own business, ja?

352
00:25:25.899 --> 00:25:27.401
Huh?

353
00:25:28.819 --> 00:25:33.699
If I want a war, then I will have it.

354
00:25:36.076 --> 00:25:37.327
As Russia's ally,

355
00:25:37.411 --> 00:25:39.455
we have no choice but to join this war.

356
00:25:39.538 --> 00:25:41.957
I don't understand.
The kaiser and the tsar

357
00:25:42.041 --> 00:25:44.460
have both ignored
the king's wishes. Why?

358
00:25:44.543 --> 00:25:45.544
That's a good question.

359
00:25:45.627 --> 00:25:47.880
- I...
- With all due respect, sir,

360
00:25:47.963 --> 00:25:49.983
this debate should happen
after we have won the war.

361
00:25:50.007 --> 00:25:51.151
The prime minister is waiting.

362
00:25:51.175 --> 00:25:52.551
And we're late.

363
00:25:53.135 --> 00:25:54.136
Morton's right.

364
00:25:54.219 --> 00:25:57.347
My lord, it would be
my honor to volunteer.

365
00:25:58.474 --> 00:25:59.725
Honor?

366
00:25:59.808 --> 00:26:01.435
Fine words, young Conrad.

367
00:26:01.518 --> 00:26:03.062
But therein lies the problem.

368
00:26:03.145 --> 00:26:05.939
Legally, you're not old enough
to join up.

369
00:26:06.023 --> 00:26:08.609
Hmm. But still young enough to believe

370
00:26:08.692 --> 00:26:11.403
it's an honorable thing
to die for one's country.

371
00:26:12.112 --> 00:26:16.241
The object of war is not
to die for one's country,

372
00:26:16.325 --> 00:26:19.411
but to make the enemy die for theirs.

373
00:26:26.752 --> 00:26:30.047
Fix bayonets!

374
00:26:58.075 --> 00:27:00.035
Not even I

375
00:27:00.119 --> 00:27:04.289
could have imagined a war like this.

376
00:27:06.291 --> 00:27:09.711
What I thought would take
a decade for us to achieve

377
00:27:10.963 --> 00:27:14.967
has taken two short years.

378
00:27:19.596 --> 00:27:23.225
We have drained Europe's resources

379
00:27:23.725 --> 00:27:27.938
and millions have died pointlessly.

380
00:27:28.021 --> 00:27:29.565
Fire!

381
00:27:29.648 --> 00:27:32.192
We have broken the trust

382
00:27:32.276 --> 00:27:35.737
between the people
and the inbred monarchs

383
00:27:35.821 --> 00:27:39.533
who only rule
due to their fortunate birth.

384
00:27:41.326 --> 00:27:43.787
Do you know who hates King George

385
00:27:43.871 --> 00:27:45.664
more than the kaiser?

386
00:27:47.499 --> 00:27:49.042
Me.

387
00:27:49.126 --> 00:27:51.795
The English monarchy

388
00:27:51.879 --> 00:27:54.756
has oppressed my beloved Scotland

389
00:27:54.840 --> 00:27:56.633
for over 700 years

390
00:27:56.717 --> 00:28:00.095
and it is time for retribution.

391
00:28:00.888 --> 00:28:04.391
We will pull Russia out of our war

392
00:28:04.474 --> 00:28:07.186
and unleash the full might of Germany

393
00:28:07.269 --> 00:28:10.272
to destroy England.

394
00:28:10.856 --> 00:28:12.482
Rasputin,

395
00:28:12.566 --> 00:28:17.863
are you ready to begin
the demise of King George?

396
00:28:17.946 --> 00:28:20.532
Thy will be done, my Shepherd.

397
00:28:27.289 --> 00:28:28.665
They've started conscription.

398
00:28:28.749 --> 00:28:30.792
Yes, I'm well aware of that, Conrad.

399
00:28:31.543 --> 00:28:32.461
And?

400
00:28:32.544 --> 00:28:34.087
Well, it was bad enough

401
00:28:34.171 --> 00:28:35.440
I didn't join when it was voluntary...

402
00:28:35.464 --> 00:28:38.050
Conrad, this is not a war.
Do you understand?

403
00:28:38.133 --> 00:28:39.843
It's not like any war
that we've ever seen.

404
00:28:39.927 --> 00:28:41.845
I don't care! I should be fighting.

405
00:28:41.929 --> 00:28:44.473
It's not fighting. It's dying.

406
00:28:46.433 --> 00:28:48.477
Much like this conversation.

407
00:28:51.104 --> 00:28:52.272
Tell that to Kitchener.

408
00:29:07.746 --> 00:29:09.539
You're still too young, Conrad.

409
00:29:12.459 --> 00:29:14.253
But everyone's lying
about their age.

410
00:29:14.336 --> 00:29:16.213
- They're all going over.
- I know.

411
00:29:16.964 --> 00:29:18.257
And I know you want to fight.

412
00:29:19.675 --> 00:29:21.301
It's a testament to your character

413
00:29:21.969 --> 00:29:23.136
and I'm proud of you for it.

414
00:29:23.220 --> 00:29:25.013
Yes, but look what I was given.

415
00:29:26.181 --> 00:29:27.181
In the village.

416
00:29:28.684 --> 00:29:30.185
It's the symbol of a coward.

417
00:29:30.269 --> 00:29:33.021
And I should suffer such humiliation?

418
00:29:34.273 --> 00:29:37.818
Reputation is what people think of you.

419
00:29:37.901 --> 00:29:40.404
Character is what you are.

420
00:29:46.868 --> 00:29:48.036
Victoria Cross.

421
00:29:49.037 --> 00:29:50.330
Is it yours?

422
00:29:51.248 --> 00:29:52.248
Yes.

423
00:29:53.125 --> 00:29:54.209
When I was young,

424
00:29:54.293 --> 00:29:57.254
like you, I wanted to serve my country.

425
00:29:59.965 --> 00:30:03.051
But soon I began
to question what right we had

426
00:30:03.135 --> 00:30:06.305
to take the land, riches,

427
00:30:06.805 --> 00:30:08.682
and the lives of people

428
00:30:08.765 --> 00:30:11.518
who were only defending their homeland.

429
00:30:14.604 --> 00:30:16.648
Everyman I killed,

430
00:30:18.150 --> 00:30:20.610
I killed a piece of myself.

431
00:30:26.992 --> 00:30:30.329
Maybe having a feather
would have been better.

432
00:30:31.997 --> 00:30:34.791
So, the next day, I put down my rifle

433
00:30:34.875 --> 00:30:36.001
and I picked up a stretcher.

434
00:30:37.210 --> 00:30:39.379
I should've been given
the Cross for saving lives,

435
00:30:39.463 --> 00:30:40.589
not taking them.

436
00:30:42.966 --> 00:30:45.510
As soon as I replace this
with my own medal,

437
00:30:46.845 --> 00:30:48.347
I'll join the medical corps.

438
00:30:51.683 --> 00:30:53.101
I have informed Kitchener

439
00:30:53.185 --> 00:30:55.062
of your intention of joining up.

440
00:30:55.562 --> 00:30:57.397
And he has assured me that he will not

441
00:30:57.481 --> 00:30:59.566
let you slip through.

442
00:31:40.899 --> 00:31:43.110
- I have a vision.

443
00:31:43.610 --> 00:31:47.030
This boy is the symbol
of the soul of Russia.

444
00:31:49.574 --> 00:31:51.660
You must save Russia.

445
00:31:53.578 --> 00:31:58.250
You must pull out of the war
to save your son's life.

446
00:31:58.333 --> 00:31:59.918
This is nonsense.

447
00:32:00.001 --> 00:32:05.132
You dare to question
the vessel of the Lord?

448
00:32:07.592 --> 00:32:12.389
You dare to risk your son's life?

449
00:32:13.432 --> 00:32:16.685
Nicholas, come to your senses now!

450
00:32:16.768 --> 00:32:18.603
Please.

451
00:32:19.729 --> 00:32:20.814
Please.

452
00:32:28.447 --> 00:32:30.282
My dear cousin Conrad.

453
00:32:30.866 --> 00:32:33.493
It has been too long
since we last saw each other

454
00:32:33.577 --> 00:32:35.704
and I'm sorry I'm only writing
to you now, but...

455
00:32:37.038 --> 00:32:39.708
in these difficult times,
I'm not sure whom I can trust.

456
00:32:46.840 --> 00:32:48.383
Welcome back.

457
00:32:50.385 --> 00:32:52.846
For a while now,
I've harbored my suspicions

458
00:32:52.929 --> 00:32:55.682
of this so-called priest, Rasputin.

459
00:32:56.349 --> 00:32:58.643
He has the tsar under his spell,

460
00:32:58.727 --> 00:33:01.480
both spiritually and through opium,

461
00:33:03.231 --> 00:33:06.568
and has persuaded him
to withdraw from the war.

462
00:33:08.195 --> 00:33:10.530
The tsar intends to announce this

463
00:33:10.614 --> 00:33:12.324
in his New Year's speech.

464
00:33:12.824 --> 00:33:14.993
Cousin Felix sends his regards.

465
00:33:15.076 --> 00:33:16.076
Oh.

466
00:33:16.119 --> 00:33:19.289
I hope your
father's influence can help.

467
00:33:20.457 --> 00:33:23.084
Morton, any ideas?

468
00:33:23.668 --> 00:33:26.129
Well, sir, in my opinion,

469
00:33:26.213 --> 00:33:27.672
this is a very grave situation.

470
00:33:27.756 --> 00:33:29.549
We can trust absolutely no one.

471
00:33:29.633 --> 00:33:31.927
I suggest we assemble
an elite squad of men,

472
00:33:32.010 --> 00:33:34.679
we go to Russia,
and we sort it out ourselves.

473
00:33:34.763 --> 00:33:36.848
Agreed. See to it immediately.

474
00:33:36.932 --> 00:33:41.061
As I'm not allowed to join up,
may I at least go with you?

475
00:33:42.812 --> 00:33:45.565
Conrad, you know your father
made me swear that I would...

476
00:33:45.649 --> 00:33:48.610
Protect my son at all costs.

477
00:33:50.487 --> 00:33:52.572
Where do you want to go, Conrad?

478
00:33:54.533 --> 00:33:56.034
- Russia.
- Why?

479
00:33:56.117 --> 00:33:58.870
To help Cousin Yusupov
deal with Rasputin.

480
00:33:58.954 --> 00:34:00.872
He's going to force Russia
out of the war.

481
00:34:01.915 --> 00:34:03.583
Kitchener, have you killed so many men

482
00:34:03.667 --> 00:34:06.103
that you're now relying on boys
to run your military intelligence?

483
00:34:06.127 --> 00:34:08.505
- How dare you speak to...
- Shut up, Morton.

484
00:34:10.966 --> 00:34:12.342
Conrad, we're leaving.

485
00:34:14.302 --> 00:34:15.595
Now!

486
00:34:26.022 --> 00:34:27.022
Your lordship?

487
00:34:27.566 --> 00:34:30.694
Let's just hope we don't make
such a mess of things in Russia.

488
00:34:40.453 --> 00:34:42.914
One more dispatch box for tonight, sir.

489
00:34:44.624 --> 00:34:45.625
Damn it, Morton.

490
00:34:45.709 --> 00:34:47.335
How much do you expect a man to read?

491
00:34:47.419 --> 00:34:48.587
I'm terribly sorry, my lord.

492
00:34:48.670 --> 00:34:51.339
I would help, but I'm definitely...

493
00:34:51.423 --> 00:34:53.925
definitely more of a soldier
than I am a sailor.

494
00:34:54.009 --> 00:34:56.052
Well, go outside, man, and get some air.

495
00:34:56.970 --> 00:34:58.138
Quite right.

496
00:36:02.786 --> 00:36:04.829
Five million dead.

497
00:36:06.539 --> 00:36:08.375
May God forgive me.

498
00:36:30.438 --> 00:36:32.691
First Ferdinand,
and now Kitchener.

499
00:36:32.774 --> 00:36:34.734
This was not an accident.

500
00:36:35.276 --> 00:36:36.316
Kitchener was your friend.

501
00:36:36.361 --> 00:36:39.072
Not to mention this country's last hope.

502
00:36:39.155 --> 00:36:40.657
How can you be so calm?

503
00:36:40.740 --> 00:36:42.367
My dear Oxford.

504
00:36:42.450 --> 00:36:45.245
I wanted to apologize
for our recent fracas.

505
00:36:45.328 --> 00:36:48.665
In my opinion,
Conrad is a fine young man.

506
00:36:48.748 --> 00:36:50.917
He was betrayed.
We must do something.

507
00:36:51.418 --> 00:36:53.128
Always ready to face the world.

508
00:36:53.211 --> 00:36:55.880
No, don't ignore me, Father.
You know it's true.

509
00:36:55.964 --> 00:36:57.841
You cannot keep running away
from problems.

510
00:36:57.924 --> 00:37:00.009
But I shall, of course,

511
00:37:00.093 --> 00:37:01.386
respect your wishes

512
00:37:01.469 --> 00:37:04.597
and do everything I can
to keep him out of harm's way.

513
00:37:04.681 --> 00:37:06.599
I don't believe it was a German mine.

514
00:37:06.683 --> 00:37:08.226
There is something more afoot.

515
00:37:10.770 --> 00:37:12.439
And what if you're successful?

516
00:37:13.231 --> 00:37:14.357
What if you're successful

517
00:37:14.441 --> 00:37:16.121
and keep me locked away
as the world burns?

518
00:37:16.151 --> 00:37:18.319
If all parents
shared your outlook,

519
00:37:18.403 --> 00:37:19.988
there would be no wars.

520
00:37:20.613 --> 00:37:25.785
But until that day comes,
I will no doubt be kept busy.

521
00:37:26.494 --> 00:37:29.247
I remain your friend, Kitch.

522
00:37:33.543 --> 00:37:35.795
Your incessant need to protect me

523
00:37:35.879 --> 00:37:38.339
will not redeem your own failure
to protect Mother.

524
00:37:44.387 --> 00:37:46.222
I'm sorry, Father.

525
00:37:58.818 --> 00:37:59.819
No, no.

526
00:38:02.781 --> 00:38:04.032
I'm sorry.

527
00:38:08.870 --> 00:38:09.996
Follow me.

528
00:38:44.823 --> 00:38:46.991
Well, about time.

529
00:38:47.575 --> 00:38:49.077
Welcome to the club.

530
00:38:49.869 --> 00:38:51.496
Is he part of the briefing?

531
00:38:51.996 --> 00:38:53.081
Yes.

532
00:38:54.958 --> 00:38:56.292
Take a look.

533
00:39:02.131 --> 00:39:04.884
You see, this war has made me realize

534
00:39:04.968 --> 00:39:07.220
that we cannot rely on politicians

535
00:39:07.303 --> 00:39:09.639
