01:00:58.530 --> 01:01:02.242
as I join up and finally
fulfill my duty to my country.

804
01:01:03.827 --> 01:01:08.039
Conrad, you've just exceeded
your duty to your country.

805
01:01:09.166 --> 01:01:12.043
My wishes have nothing
to do with your age.

806
01:01:12.127 --> 01:01:15.380
Father, your wishes were only granted
because of my age.

807
01:01:16.339 --> 01:01:18.800
There's nothing you can do
to stop me now.

808
01:01:19.718 --> 01:01:22.637
All I ask for is your blessing,
at least.

809
01:01:25.724 --> 01:01:27.392
I'm sorry, Conrad.

810
01:01:27.976 --> 01:01:30.061
But you're asking for the one thing

811
01:01:30.145 --> 01:01:33.148
that I cannot and I will not give you.

812
01:02:25.075 --> 01:02:26.284
My kaiser.

813
01:02:26.368 --> 01:02:28.536
Our naval blockade around England

814
01:02:28.620 --> 01:02:30.789
has sunk another
American passenger ship.

815
01:02:30.872 --> 01:02:33.875
The American president
could soon run out of patience

816
01:02:33.959 --> 01:02:36.461
and if they join the war
on England's side,

817
01:02:37.128 --> 01:02:38.380
we will be defeated.

818
01:02:38.463 --> 01:02:41.007
There are no rules in war.

819
01:02:41.091 --> 01:02:44.761
And making England
starve to death is worth the risk.

820
01:02:44.844 --> 01:02:45.929
Hmm...

821
01:02:46.471 --> 01:02:48.556
But if you send this,

822
01:02:48.640 --> 01:02:51.142
it will mitigate the risk.

823
01:02:56.898 --> 01:02:58.108
Are you sure?

824
01:02:58.191 --> 01:02:59.985
Yes, my kaiser.

825
01:03:04.072 --> 01:03:05.115
Get me Zimmermann.

826
01:03:07.117 --> 01:03:09.327
Zimmermann, telegraph the following.

827
01:03:16.042 --> 01:03:17.794
Send this immediately.

828
01:03:17.877 --> 01:03:20.880
Use the kaiser's top-level encoding.

829
01:03:24.718 --> 01:03:25.802
Gentlemen,

830
01:03:25.885 --> 01:03:28.263
we have a priority-one intercept.

831
01:03:28.346 --> 01:03:31.016
Whatever you're doing, cease now.

832
01:03:31.099 --> 01:03:33.059
We need this code cracked pronto.

833
01:03:36.646 --> 01:03:38.273
- Tea?
- Please.

834
01:03:47.073 --> 01:03:48.366
Good job, Rita.

835
01:03:48.450 --> 01:03:50.785
This code is what
the kaiser has been using.

836
01:03:50.869 --> 01:03:53.079
It must be unbelievably important.

837
01:03:53.163 --> 01:03:54.497
Can you break it?

838
01:03:55.498 --> 01:03:59.002
One! Two! Three! Four!

839
01:03:59.085 --> 01:04:01.296
I'll need a lot more information.

840
01:04:01.379 --> 01:04:03.548
Keep your eye on the enemy!

841
01:04:03.631 --> 01:04:04.758
Aim rifles to the left!

842
01:04:04.841 --> 01:04:05.841
Fire!

843
01:04:06.551 --> 01:04:07.844
Thank you.

844
01:04:08.428 --> 01:04:10.263
What makes the grass grow?

845
01:04:10.347 --> 01:04:12.307
Blood! Blood! Blood!

846
01:04:13.224 --> 01:04:14.309
What're you gonna do?

847
01:04:14.392 --> 01:04:15.935
Kill! Kill! Kill!

848
01:04:18.938 --> 01:04:19.981
Here's your tea.

849
01:04:21.858 --> 01:04:23.485
Quick! March!

850
01:04:26.821 --> 01:04:28.281
Mmm-hmm. Ja.

851
01:04:28.365 --> 01:04:30.742
I am using the cipher.

852
01:04:30.825 --> 01:04:33.453
Is the eight a "Z" or is it an "R"?

853
01:04:37.624 --> 01:04:39.042
Godspeed to you all.

854
01:04:39.125 --> 01:04:40.835
And remember...

855
01:04:40.919 --> 01:04:44.839
"Dulce et decorum
est pro patria mori."

856
01:04:44.923 --> 01:04:46.132
What does that mean?

857
01:04:46.216 --> 01:04:48.968
"It's sweet and proper
to die for one's country."

858
01:04:51.805 --> 01:04:53.932
Direct from Germany.

859
01:04:54.015 --> 01:04:55.183
Thank you.

860
01:05:01.689 --> 01:05:04.275
Ja. I am using the cipher.

861
01:05:04.359 --> 01:05:07.737
Is the eight a "Z" or is it an "R"?

862
01:05:09.656 --> 01:05:12.450
A "Z." Thank you.

863
01:05:23.086 --> 01:05:24.504
I've cracked the code.

864
01:05:25.046 --> 01:05:27.566
It's from Arthur Zimmermann,
the German Secretary of State in Berlin

865
01:05:27.590 --> 01:05:29.759
to their ambassador in Mexico City.

866
01:05:29.843 --> 01:05:32.095
He proposes an alliance with Mexico.

867
01:05:32.178 --> 01:05:35.140
Germany wants to divert
America's attention,

868
01:05:35.223 --> 01:05:37.684
so they're asking Mexico
to invade America.

869
01:05:37.767 --> 01:05:38.977
In print, there.

870
01:05:39.060 --> 01:05:42.313
So, when President Wilson sees this,
then he has no choice but...

871
01:05:43.064 --> 01:05:44.357
He has to enter the war.

872
01:05:44.441 --> 01:05:46.192
And the war will be over.

873
01:05:46.860 --> 01:05:49.529
- Well done. Oh, my dear Polly.

874
01:05:49.612 --> 01:05:51.281
Well done, you.

875
01:05:53.116 --> 01:05:54.576
You are incredible.

876
01:05:55.535 --> 01:05:57.537
And there's hope for Conrad.

877
01:06:02.167 --> 01:06:03.835
Well done, Oxford.

878
01:06:03.918 --> 01:06:06.087
My idiot cousin, the kaiser,

879
01:06:06.171 --> 01:06:08.214
has finally shot himself in the foot.

880
01:06:08.298 --> 01:06:10.508
You've hit a six
with this telegram, old boy.

881
01:06:10.592 --> 01:06:11.759
Kitchener would be proud.

882
01:06:13.386 --> 01:06:15.346
Well, I think champagne is in order.

883
01:06:15.430 --> 01:06:18.558
Uh, thank you, Your Majesty,
but I vowed not to drink

884
01:06:18.641 --> 01:06:22.812
until Conrad has returned
safely from the war.

885
01:06:22.896 --> 01:06:24.522
Why didn't you mention that earlier?

886
01:06:25.064 --> 01:06:27.150
I'll make sure the only action
your boy sees

887
01:06:27.233 --> 01:06:29.110
is sharpening the general's pencils.

888
01:06:29.194 --> 01:06:32.572
I'm not sure that's cricket.

889
01:06:36.117 --> 01:06:38.244
Orlando, you know how many
boys' lives you've saved

890
01:06:38.328 --> 01:06:39.370
with this telegram?

891
01:06:40.121 --> 01:06:41.831
At least let me save one.

892
01:06:45.376 --> 01:06:46.753
So,

893
01:06:47.629 --> 01:06:49.839
now that Conrad's safety is assured...

894
01:06:52.175 --> 01:06:53.885
to peace in our time.

895
01:06:54.677 --> 01:06:56.763
To peace in our time.

896
01:06:58.348 --> 01:07:01.267
King George is waiting
for your response, Mr. President.

897
01:07:01.351 --> 01:07:03.811
But how can this telegram be real?

898
01:07:03.895 --> 01:07:05.897
Not even the Germans
would be this stupid.

899
01:07:05.980 --> 01:07:08.775
- But, sir...
- I'm not doing a damn thing

900
01:07:08.858 --> 01:07:10.818
till I have undeniable proof.

901
01:07:10.902 --> 01:07:12.278
Douglas.

902
01:07:13.112 --> 01:07:15.031
Statesman on the rocks, please.

903
01:07:22.872 --> 01:07:25.291
Lieutenant Oxford reporting
for duty, sir.

904
01:07:26.501 --> 01:07:28.545
Ah, yes. Oxford.

905
01:07:29.295 --> 01:07:32.549
Lucky man. You've been
assigned back to London.

906
01:07:35.301 --> 01:07:37.512
Sir, there must be some mistake.

907
01:07:37.595 --> 01:07:39.514
No. Fortune favors the brave,

908
01:07:40.473 --> 01:07:42.600
or those under the king's gaze.

909
01:07:46.771 --> 01:07:47.939
Sir.

910
01:07:50.149 --> 01:07:51.234
Attention!

911
01:08:12.171 --> 01:08:13.673
Lance corporal.

912
01:08:13.756 --> 01:08:15.717
- Sir.
- What's your name?

913
01:08:15.800 --> 01:08:17.302
Lance Corporal Reid, sir.

914
01:08:18.136 --> 01:08:19.136
Follow me.

915
01:08:35.320 --> 01:08:37.280
Shola, I presume.

916
01:08:38.698 --> 01:08:39.698
Yes.

917
01:08:39.741 --> 01:08:42.118
Conrad has sent me to see the duke.

918
01:08:44.621 --> 01:08:45.622
And your name, sir?

919
01:08:46.372 --> 01:08:50.918
Good question.
It's a complicated answer.

920
01:08:51.002 --> 01:08:52.712
I can only tell the duke in person.

921
01:08:52.795 --> 01:08:54.547
Well, I still need a name.

922
01:08:54.631 --> 01:08:56.466
This is gonna sound stupid.

923
01:08:57.175 --> 01:08:59.260
But according to Conrad,
I'm Lancelot.

924
01:08:59.969 --> 01:09:01.638
You're Merlin,

925
01:09:01.721 --> 01:09:04.265
and I'm requesting an audience
with King Arthur.

926
01:09:05.683 --> 01:09:07.226
Follow me, sir.

927
01:09:10.063 --> 01:09:13.399
"Doubts persist
as to telegram authenticity.

928
01:09:13.483 --> 01:09:16.319
"Worried Wilson won't go to war."

929
01:09:16.402 --> 01:09:17.487
Idiots and fools.

930
01:09:17.570 --> 01:09:19.280
There's nothing left to debate.

931
01:09:20.698 --> 01:09:23.451
Polly, do you think
we can extend our network

932
01:09:23.534 --> 01:09:24.535
to the White House?

933
01:09:25.161 --> 01:09:27.288
Most of their household staff
were trained in England,

934
01:09:27.372 --> 01:09:28.515
so it shouldn't be a problem.

935
01:09:28.539 --> 01:09:30.017
Right. Well, let's get to work, then.

936
01:09:30.041 --> 01:09:32.210
- I'll get on to it right away.
- Thank you.

937
01:09:38.341 --> 01:09:39.425
Yes, come in.

938
01:09:41.469 --> 01:09:44.055
Your Grace. We have a visitor.

939
01:09:44.138 --> 01:09:45.390
Who is it?

940
01:09:46.015 --> 01:09:48.518
A friend of Conrad saying he's Lancelot,

941
01:09:48.601 --> 01:09:50.144
asking to see King Arthur.

942
01:09:50.228 --> 01:09:52.021
What?

943
01:09:52.105 --> 01:09:53.898
That brings back fond memories.

944
01:09:53.981 --> 01:09:55.066
Um...

945
01:09:55.692 --> 01:09:56.693
Show him in, would you?

946
01:09:56.776 --> 01:09:57.985
Yes, sir.

947
01:09:58.861 --> 01:09:59.862
Sir.

948
01:10:02.448 --> 01:10:03.533
Who are you?

949
01:10:03.616 --> 01:10:06.327
Lance Corporal Reid
of the Black Watch, sir.

950
01:10:07.286 --> 01:10:10.081
So then why are you wearing
a Grenadiers officer's uniform?

951
01:10:12.834 --> 01:10:13.835
This, uh...

952
01:10:15.712 --> 01:10:17.964
This will explain it better than I can.

953
01:10:18.047 --> 01:10:20.174
It's a wee bit surreal, sir.

954
01:10:24.637 --> 01:10:25.638
Hmm.

955
01:10:26.723 --> 01:10:27.890
Odd.

956
01:10:27.974 --> 01:10:30.643
It's a letter from Conrad.

957
01:10:31.811 --> 01:10:33.229
You're Lancelot.

958
01:10:35.273 --> 01:10:38.484
Dear Father.
I, too, can play games.

959
01:10:39.610 --> 01:10:42.113
I've swapped places with Archie Reid,

960
01:10:42.613 --> 01:10:43.990
the man in front of you.

961
01:10:44.574 --> 01:10:45.658
Archie?

962
01:10:45.742 --> 01:10:47.493
He's a goodman...
- Yes, sir.

963
01:10:47.577 --> 01:10:49.454
Who is simply following my orders

964
01:10:49.537 --> 01:10:51.998
and is possibly as confused as you are.

965
01:10:52.790 --> 01:10:54.125
Please ensure my actions

966
01:10:54.208 --> 01:10:55.835
don't get him into any trouble.

967
01:10:56.544 --> 01:11:00.006
Tomorrow I finally fulfill
my wish to go to the front.

968
01:11:00.840 --> 01:11:03.092
Andin the meantime, I enclose a poem

969
01:11:03.926 --> 01:11:06.053
which I thought you might appreciate.

970
01:11:07.555 --> 01:11:08.639
"Bent double...

971
01:11:10.141 --> 01:11:13.019
"like old beggars under sacks...

972
01:11:14.729 --> 01:11:18.441
"Knock-kneed, coughing like hags...

973
01:11:19.984 --> 01:11:22.487
"we cursed through sludge...

974
01:11:23.571 --> 01:11:27.742
"Till on the haunting flares
we turned our backs...

975
01:11:28.868 --> 01:11:34.248
"And towards our distant rest
began to trudge.

976
01:11:39.003 --> 01:11:41.547
"Men marched asleep.

977
01:11:42.590 --> 01:11:46.219
"Many had lost their boots,
but limped on...

978
01:11:47.011 --> 01:11:48.554
"blood-shod.

979
01:11:50.389 --> 01:11:54.769
"All went lame, all blind.

980
01:11:55.812 --> 01:11:58.064
"Drunk with fatigue...

981
01:11:58.564 --> 01:12:00.650
"deaf even to the hoots...

982
01:12:00.733 --> 01:12:04.612
"Of tired outstripped five-nines

983
01:12:04.695 --> 01:12:06.405
"that dropped behind."

984
01:12:14.205 --> 01:12:15.206
New lads.

985
01:12:15.289 --> 01:12:16.958
Welcome to the front line.

986
01:12:17.041 --> 01:12:18.393
This trench will be your home
for the next six...

987
01:12:18.417 --> 01:12:20.962
I don't bloody believe it. Runner!

988
01:12:21.629 --> 01:12:23.339
Come on, lads!

989
01:12:34.100 --> 01:12:36.018
Well, come on, lads! Cover the man!

990
01:12:38.312 --> 01:12:40.314
Cover the man!

991
01:12:44.193 --> 01:12:45.193
Fire!

992
01:12:46.654 --> 01:12:47.655
Keep running!

993
01:12:53.661 --> 01:12:55.246
Hold your fire!

994
01:13:01.544 --> 01:13:02.879
Good effort, men.

995
01:13:03.754 --> 01:13:06.048
This war never stops surprising me.

996
01:13:06.549 --> 01:13:09.844
A German wavin' a Union Jack!
What's next?

997
01:13:10.678 --> 01:13:12.305
Allow me
to answer that, Sergeant Major.

998
01:13:12.388 --> 01:13:13.931
Fall in!

999
01:13:16.767 --> 01:13:19.478
That runner was actually a British spy.

1000
01:13:19.562 --> 01:13:21.188
He was bringing me vital information.

1001
01:13:21.898 --> 01:13:23.250
Our country needs what he was carrying,

1002
01:13:23.274 --> 01:13:25.443
and I therefore need six volunteers.

1003
01:13:26.110 --> 01:13:28.130
You will accompany me
to retrieve what's left of him

1004
01:13:28.154 --> 01:13:30.239
as soon as it's dark.

1005
01:13:34.076 --> 01:13:35.202
Very good, lad.

1006
01:13:36.621 --> 01:13:37.705
Who else?

1007
01:13:39.832 --> 01:13:40.875
Sergeant?

1008
01:13:42.168 --> 01:13:44.962
You five. One step forward. March!

1009
01:13:46.964 --> 01:13:49.133
Five more brave volunteers, sir.

1010
01:13:49.216 --> 01:13:52.678
Excellent. We move out at midnight.

1011
01:14:33.427 --> 01:14:34.553
Hold your fire.

1012
01:14:35.388 --> 01:14:39.225
If they hear us from the trenches,
we'll be fired upon from both sides.

1013
01:14:54.448 --> 01:14:56.158
Boom.

1014
01:16:12.276 --> 01:16:13.486
Please...

1015
01:16:14.612 --> 01:16:16.530
- Please don't.

1016
01:16:30.628 --> 01:16:31.670
I'm so sorry.

1017
01:17:02.868 --> 01:17:04.120
What was that?

1018
01:17:28.352 --> 01:17:29.353
It's over there.

1019
01:17:29.436 --> 01:17:30.813
Don't shoot!

1020
01:17:33.107 --> 01:17:34.358
No!

1021
01:18:13.981 --> 01:18:16.275
Cease fire!

1022
01:18:41.133 --> 01:18:42.718
First time out here, lad?

1023
01:18:43.802 --> 01:18:45.387
Hey. Whoa, whoa, whoa.

1024
01:18:47.223 --> 01:18:48.974
Same side.

1025
01:18:49.767 --> 01:18:51.310
Thank God for the Union Jack, eh?

1026
01:18:55.773 --> 01:18:57.775
I can honestly say that my first time

1027
01:18:57.858 --> 01:18:59.568
was worse than losing this leg.

1028
01:19:02.446 --> 01:19:05.950
I'm so sorry, I shouldn't
be the one crying.

1029
01:19:06.033 --> 01:19:08.452
Come over here and help me out.
I'm freezing.

1030
01:19:14.375 --> 01:19:17.169
Come here. Come on.

1031
01:19:25.469 --> 01:19:28.514
I thought... I thought I knew
what I wanted.

1032
01:19:35.479 --> 01:19:37.731
My father warned me.

1033
01:19:38.816 --> 01:19:41.694
My father warned me.
I... I didn't listen...

1034
01:19:43.529 --> 01:19:45.489
and now it all makes sense.

1035
01:19:49.994 --> 01:19:52.454
I didn't even get to say goodbye.

1036
01:19:53.664 --> 01:19:57.793
Well, I suggest we solve
both our problems, yeah?

1037
01:19:58.419 --> 01:19:59.795
Look.

1038
01:20:00.629 --> 01:20:02.548
I need to get this to high command.

1039
01:20:03.048 --> 01:20:05.551
The contents could help
end this bloody war.

1040
01:20:06.593 --> 01:20:09.888
As I won't be walking any time soon,

1041
01:20:11.181 --> 01:20:13.892
I suggest you finish the mission

1042
01:20:16.186 --> 01:20:18.314
and go home to a hero's welcome.

1043
01:20:18.856 --> 01:20:23.652
No, no. No. Off we go
to a hero's welcome.

1044
01:20:43.630 --> 01:20:46.091
- It's okay. I've got you.

1045
01:20:55.059 --> 01:20:57.311
Shit. Hurry!

1046
01:20:59.563 --> 01:21:01.774
Covering fire!

1047
01:21:01.857 --> 01:21:03.108
Give them cover, lads!

1048
01:21:06.570 --> 01:21:08.322
Fucking move!

1049
01:21:11.325 --> 01:21:13.118
Take out the machine gunner!

1050
01:21:13.202 --> 01:21:14.828
Cover him!

1051
01:21:20.584 --> 01:21:23.212
Go!

1052
01:21:23.295 --> 01:21:25.964
Run!

1053
01:21:26.048 --> 01:21:29.093
Let's go, man! Run!
Run! Run! Run!

1054
01:22:08.006 --> 01:22:10.050
You all right? You all right?

1055
01:22:10.592 --> 01:22:12.886
Jesus Christ! You were amazin'!

1056
01:22:12.970 --> 01:22:14.805
I've never seen anything like it.

1057
01:22:14.888 --> 01:22:17.488
What the bloody hell were you doing
over there in the first place?

1058
01:22:18.851 --> 01:22:20.853
You better ask him. Ask him.

1059
01:22:21.437 --> 01:22:23.313
He'll explain everything.

1060
01:22:24.106 --> 01:22:26.108
He took the full force
of that blast, sir.

1061
01:22:26.191 --> 01:22:28.444
Yeah. But at least
you made it back, son.

1062
01:22:29.027 --> 01:22:31.738
I tell you, if that ain't worth
a Victoria Cross,

1063
01:22:31.822 --> 01:22:32.906
I don't know what is.

1064
01:22:32.990 --> 01:22:34.491
I must carry on the mission.

1065
01:22:34.575 --> 01:22:36.869
We need to get this
to high command immediately.

1066
01:22:36.952 --> 01:22:39.788
I'll take you there myself.
What's your name, soldier?

1067
01:22:40.998 --> 01:22:44.042
Archie. Lance Corporal Archie Reid.

1068
01:22:44.126 --> 01:22:45.752
Archie Reid, did you say?

1069
01:22:46.628 --> 01:22:47.628
Yes.

1070
01:22:48.213 --> 01:22:49.381
That's right.

1071
01:22:49.465 --> 01:22:50.966
Lance Corporal Archie Reid?

1072
01:22:51.842 --> 01:22:53.927
Dog Platoon, First Battalion,
the Black Watch?

1073
01:22:54.845 --> 01:22:55.846
Aye.

1074
01:22:58.140 --> 01:22:59.933
Is that your best Scottish accent?

1075
01:23:00.434 --> 01:23:01.435
You're not Archie Reid.

1076
01:23:02.144 --> 01:23:04.188
Lance Corporal Archie Reid's
a friend of mine.

1077
01:23:04.271 --> 01:23:06.124
And I've been looking for him all night.
So who are you?

1078
01:23:06.148 --> 01:23:10.152
Yes, yes. You're right.
There's a simple explanation.

1079
01:23:10.235 --> 01:23:12.029
- I'm not Archie Reid.
- Fuckin' German spy.

1080
01:23:12.112 --> 01:23:13.238
I'm Conra...

1081
01:23:34.718 --> 01:23:36.261
Your son was killed in action, sir.

1082
01:23:49.441 --> 01:23:50.441
What?

1083
01:24:33.902 --> 01:24:34.987
Polly.

1084
01:24:38.407 --> 01:24:39.575
Polly.

1085
01:24:51.503 --> 01:24:53.005
My son.

1086
01:25:03.348 --> 01:25:04.808
Why?

1087
01:25:16.695 --> 01:25:20.824
"If in some smothering dreams...

1088
01:25:20.907 --> 01:25:22.701
"you too could pace

1089
01:25:22.784 --> 01:25:25.537
"Behind the wagon
that we flung him in...

1090
01:25:26.371 --> 01:25:30.876
"And watch the white eyes
writhing in his face...

1091
01:25:33.503 --> 01:25:38.717
"His hanging face,
like a devil's sick of sin...

1092
01:25:39.426 --> 01:25:42.638
"If you could hear, at every jolt...

1093
01:25:42.721 --> 01:25:47.184
"the blood, come gargling
from the froth-corrupted lungs...

1094
01:25:48.644 --> 01:25:51.229
"Obscene as cancer...

1095
01:25:52.272 --> 01:25:54.316
"bitter as the cud...

1096
01:25:54.983 --> 01:26:00.197
"Of vile, incurable sores
on innocent tongues...

1097
01:26:01.448 --> 01:26:02.741
"My friend...

1098
01:26:03.950 --> 01:26:08.246
"you would not tell
with such high zest...

1099
01:26:08.330 --> 01:26:10.957
"To children ardent for...

1100
01:26:11.708 --> 01:26:13.960
"some desperate glory...

1101
01:26:14.044 --> 01:26:15.837
"The old Lie...

1102
01:26:17.381 --> 01:26:20.425
"Dulce et decorum est...

1103
01:26:21.510 --> 01:26:24.012
"Pro patria mori."

1104
01:26:25.972 --> 01:26:29.017
It is sweet and proper

1105
01:26:29.893 --> 01:26:33.313
to die for one's country.

1106
01:26:50.831 --> 01:26:54.209
I, Nikolai Aleksandrovich Romanov,

1107
01:26:54.292 --> 01:26:56.586
Emperor of Russia,

1108
01:26:56.670 --> 01:26:59.089
do hereby declare
my irrevocable determination

1109
01:26:59.172 --> 01:27:01.258
to renounce the throne for myself

1110
01:27:01.341 --> 01:27:02.426
and my descendants

1111
01:27:02.509 --> 01:27:05.846
through this instrument of abdication...

1112
01:27:07.681 --> 01:27:09.224
immediately.

1113
01:27:17.566 --> 01:27:19.526
Hurrah! Hurrah! Hurrah!

1114
01:27:35.584 --> 01:27:37.586
The documents Conrad recovered

1115
01:27:38.420 --> 01:27:40.255
turned out to be
the German ambassador's

1116
01:27:40.338 --> 01:27:43.633
original handwritten telegram
that I cracked.

1117
01:27:44.634 --> 01:27:47.179
It's the concrete proof America needed.

1118
01:27:47.888 --> 01:27:50.932
America will now
have to join the war.

1119
01:27:51.016 --> 01:27:54.019
Conrad succeeded where we all failed.

1120
01:28:04.863 --> 01:28:05.989
My Shepherd.

1121
01:28:07.282 --> 01:28:08.575
There is a code of honor

1122
01:28:08.658 --> 01:28:11.828
and using a distraction
to your own advantage

1123
01:28:11.912 --> 01:28:13.580
breaks that code.

1124
01:28:13.663 --> 01:28:15.290
- What?
- Apologies, my Shepherd,

1125
01:28:15.373 --> 01:28:17.209
but I have disturbing news.

1126
01:28:17.292 --> 01:28:20.796
While your plan for Russia
has been a great success,

1127
01:28:20.879 --> 01:28:24.549
my plan to keep America
out of the war has backfired.

1128
01:28:25.175 --> 01:28:26.384
The American president

1129
01:28:26.468 --> 01:28:28.178
is about to be given the actual telegram

1130
01:28:28.261 --> 01:28:29.679
I forced the kaiser to send.

1131
01:28:29.763 --> 01:28:31.681
Such undeniable proof

1132
01:28:31.765 --> 01:28:34.392
could provoke the Americans
into entering the war.

1133
01:28:39.815 --> 01:28:41.066
En garde.

1134
01:28:46.780 --> 01:28:50.158
I like a man who will admit
to his mistakes, I do.

1135
01:28:50.242 --> 01:28:54.788
But I like more a woman
who can fix them.

1136
01:28:54.871 --> 01:28:57.582
Have our American friend Dupont

1137
01:28:57.666 --> 01:28:59.584
get Mata into the White House.

1138
01:28:59.668 --> 01:29:01.753
Time for you to work your magic

1139
01:29:01.837 --> 01:29:04.047
on the president, Mata.

1140
01:29:04.130 --> 01:29:05.549
Now, go on.

1141
01:29:06.633 --> 01:29:08.260
It's time to show the president

1142
01:29:09.052 --> 01:29:11.555
who the real boss is.

1143
01:29:21.147 --> 01:29:22.482
Will Your Grace be having tea?

1144
01:29:25.944 --> 01:29:27.696
It's scotch time.

1145
01:29:28.613 --> 01:29:30.198
Twenty-four hours a day.

1146
01:30:07.444 --> 01:30:09.070
- For the last time,

1147
01:30:09.154 --> 01:30:10.614
I don't want any fucking tea!

1148
01:30:10.697 --> 01:30:12.115
Neither do I.

1149
01:30:13.658 --> 01:30:14.826
Sir.

1150
01:30:17.787 --> 01:30:20.957
Though it looks like you could
use a strong one to sober up.

1151
01:30:22.375 --> 01:30:24.252
I'm afraid it'll take
more than that, sir.

1152
01:30:24.336 --> 01:30:26.880
Oh, well, maybe this will do the trick.

1153
01:30:26.963 --> 01:30:28.757
Russia's pulled out of the war.

1154
01:30:29.633 --> 01:30:32.052
The British Empire
faces imminent defeat.

1155
01:30:32.886 --> 01:30:35.513
America still refuses to join.

1156
01:30:36.556 --> 01:30:39.476
I personally telephoned
President Wilson.

1157
01:30:40.894 --> 01:30:42.979
He didn't deign to receive my call.

1158
01:30:43.063 --> 01:30:45.982
Hmm. So, they got to him as well.

1159
01:30:46.066 --> 01:30:47.943
Indeed.
- Hmm.

1160
01:30:48.610 --> 01:30:50.528
The kaiser's blockade is working.

1161
01:30:51.363 --> 01:30:53.073
The people are hungry.

1162
01:30:53.865 --> 01:30:56.868
The next revolution might be here.

1163
01:30:58.495 --> 01:31:01.039
I've even been advised
to change my German surname

1164
01:31:01.122 --> 01:31:03.708
Saxe-Coburg to Windsor.

1165
01:31:04.334 --> 01:31:05.627
More English.

1166
01:31:08.129 --> 01:31:09.965
I'm afraid, then, sir,

1167
01:31:10.507 --> 01:31:12.550
that England is doomed.

1168
01:31:19.975 --> 01:31:21.601
I wanted to give you this.

1169
01:31:23.061 --> 01:31:24.062
For Conrad.

1170
01:31:24.896 --> 01:31:27.482
A true hero.

1171
01:31:29.651 --> 01:31:32.070
A man who knew his duty.

1172
01:31:43.331 --> 01:31:46.751
Enough of this self-pitying poppycock.

1173
01:31:47.419 --> 01:31:48.586
If it were just you...

1174
01:31:49.212 --> 01:31:53.425
you and I, in our grief,
I'd say do as you will.

1175
01:31:53.508 --> 01:31:57.429
Drown in drink, and I'd join you.

1176
01:31:58.471 --> 01:32:00.015
But he's watching.

1177
01:32:02.434 --> 01:32:05.145
And he would have been
such a better man.

1178
01:32:09.524 --> 01:32:11.067
But he can't.

1179
01:32:12.277 --> 01:32:16.072
He won't be that. Not anymore.

1180
01:32:16.656 --> 01:32:20.827
So, you must, in his stead,

1181
01:32:22.495 --> 01:32:25.498
be the man your son would have been.

1182
01:32:32.380 --> 01:32:35.341
Regretfully, I can no longer
remain in your service.

1183
01:32:37.218 --> 01:32:38.678
Forgive me, my lady.

1184
01:32:47.479 --> 01:32:49.439
My heart is broken as well.

1185
01:32:50.565 --> 01:32:52.942
Polly. Polly.

1186
01:32:54.903 --> 01:32:56.696
I do not accept your resignation.

1187
01:32:59.407 --> 01:33:00.909
But...

1188
01:33:01.868 --> 01:33:05.997
I will accept a very strong cup of tea.

1189
01:33:39.030 --> 01:33:40.110
Looking better, Your Grace.

1190
01:33:42.117 --> 01:33:43.827
Feeling better, Polly.

1191
01:33:45.745 --> 01:33:46.871
So, what have I missed?

1192
01:33:47.455 --> 01:33:49.749
We followed your last sober order

1193
01:33:49.833 --> 01:33:53.044
and extended our network
to the White House.

1194
01:33:53.128 --> 01:33:54.838
The president's butler informed us

1195
01:33:54.921 --> 01:33:57.132
that since receiving
the telegram Conrad recovered,

1196
01:33:57.215 --> 01:33:59.342
the president hasn't been himself.

1197
01:33:59.425 --> 01:34:01.511
This may be the proof I asked for.

1198
01:34:01.594 --> 01:34:02.971
But remember my election promise.

1199
01:34:03.054 --> 01:34:04.931
Out of the war, not in.

1200
01:34:05.014 --> 01:34:07.767
Douglas, get me a Statesman
on the rocks, now!

1201
01:34:07.851 --> 01:34:09.018
Constantly engaged

1202
01:34:09.102 --> 01:34:11.646
in top-secret conversations
with his embassy in London.

1203
01:34:11.729 --> 01:34:14.190
And ignoring all advice to go to war.

1204
01:34:14.274 --> 01:34:16.442
And do we have someone in the embassy?

1205
01:34:16.526 --> 01:34:17.694
Of course.

1206
01:34:18.278 --> 01:34:19.278
Mr. President...

1207
01:34:19.320 --> 01:34:20.989
I don't know how to proceed.

1208
01:34:21.072 --> 01:34:23.867
We're meeting to discuss
her new demands.

1209
01:34:23.950 --> 01:34:25.493
- I see.
- She was very convincing.

1210
01:34:25.577 --> 01:34:28.371
And she suggests we make
an unannounced visit at 3:00.

1211
01:34:28.454 --> 01:34:32.041
Right, well. We had better
get a move on, then.

1212
01:34:46.347 --> 01:34:47.515
Good afternoon.

1213
01:34:47.599 --> 01:34:48.933
Please inform the ambassador

1214
01:34:49.017 --> 01:34:50.810
the Duke of Oxford is here to see him.

1215
01:34:52.687 --> 01:34:54.105
Yes, Your Grace.

1216
01:34:55.481 --> 01:34:56.900
Mr. Ambassador.

1217
01:35:02.488 --> 01:35:03.865
Why did you kill my friend?

1218
01:35:04.449 --> 01:35:05.867
It was the alcohol.

1219
01:35:05.950 --> 01:35:06.951
I was overcome.

1220
01:35:08.328 --> 01:35:10.371
Thank you for your time,
Mr. Ambassador.

1221
01:35:13.958 --> 01:35:15.043
Hmm.

1222
01:35:17.503 --> 01:35:19.672
If you wouldn't mind...

1223
01:35:20.465 --> 01:35:23.801
I'm sorry. I couldn't help
admiring your scarf.

1224
01:35:23.885 --> 01:35:25.678
An exquisite cashmere.

1225
01:35:25.762 --> 01:35:27.138
Yes, it's very rare.

1226
01:35:27.222 --> 01:35:30.141
Hmm. Do you know the test
of a truly pure cashmere?

1227
01:35:31.559 --> 01:35:32.810
- A ring.
- Mmm-hmm.

1228
01:35:32.894 --> 01:35:37.023
Yet, happily, you do not wear one.

1229
01:35:37.774 --> 01:35:39.734
You are

1230
01:35:41.069 --> 01:35:42.070
mistaken.

1231
01:35:42.153 --> 01:35:43.905
Now that

1232
01:35:45.114 --> 01:35:46.324
is disappointing.

1233
01:35:46.407 --> 01:35:47.992
But this

1234
01:35:49.494 --> 01:35:50.494
is not.

1235
01:36:02.799 --> 01:36:04.634
I believe it's ungentlemanly
to hurt a woman,

1236
01:36:04.717 --> 01:36:05.957
but since the fate of the world

1237
01:36:06.010 --> 01:36:08.012
hangs in the balance,
I'm going to bend the rules.

1238
01:36:08.096 --> 01:36:09.305
Now tell me who's behind this,

1239
01:36:09.389 --> 01:36:12.183
or so help me,
you'll never breathe again.

1240
01:36:13.351 --> 01:36:15.561
You will have to kill me.

1241
01:36:25.113 --> 01:36:27.490
Ah... Ambassador.

1242
01:36:29.158 --> 01:36:30.910
- Is she dead?
- No.

1243
01:36:31.411 --> 01:36:34.038
She has an extreme case of hypoxia.

1244
01:36:34.122 --> 01:36:36.124
She'll be fine, and so will you,

1245
01:36:36.207 --> 01:36:38.793
as long as we have
an honest conversation.

1246
01:36:46.718 --> 01:36:48.052
What you're lookin' at

1247
01:36:48.136 --> 01:36:50.430
is the lady you strangled.

1248
01:36:50.513 --> 01:36:53.182
She filmed herself
seducing the president

1249
01:36:53.266 --> 01:36:54.976
and is now blackmailing us

1250
01:36:55.059 --> 01:36:57.895
to not even think
about entering the war.

1251
01:36:57.979 --> 01:37:01.607
We cannot risk the integrity
of the U.S. presidency.

1252
01:37:01.691 --> 01:37:02.984
I'm sure.

1253
01:37:03.067 --> 01:37:06.070
Now, if we can get that negative,

1254
01:37:06.154 --> 01:37:08.072
then we will happily join England

1255
01:37:08.156 --> 01:37:10.074
and put Germany out of business.

1256
01:37:10.158 --> 01:37:12.410
Well, I suggest you interrogate her.

1257
01:37:12.994 --> 01:37:16.247
And I'll follow up on this.

1258
01:37:18.708 --> 01:37:21.753
This is cashmere from the Kamaliro goat.

1259
01:37:22.712 --> 01:37:23.713
It's very rare.

1260
01:37:24.547 --> 01:37:25.548
Where does it come from?

1261
01:37:26.507 --> 01:37:29.218
Mr. Collins,
cashmere book number one, please.

1262
01:37:31.596 --> 01:37:32.597
Thank you.

1263
01:37:33.890 --> 01:37:36.559
It comes from here.

1264
01:37:36.642 --> 01:37:38.144
The only place in the world

1265
01:37:38.227 --> 01:37:40.355
where the Kamaliro goat breeds.

1266
01:37:40.438 --> 01:37:42.440
Excellent. Shola,

1267
01:37:42.940 --> 01:37:45.443
we're going into the cashmere business.

1268
01:38:03.169 --> 01:38:06.381
I can see six men guarding the lift.

1269
01:38:07.256 --> 01:38:08.508
Ah...

1270
01:38:08.591 --> 01:38:09.884
If you can call it that.

1271
01:38:09.967 --> 01:38:13.012
Give the word and their numbers
will be reduced.

1272
01:38:13.596 --> 01:38:14.597
Oh, no, Polly.

1273
01:38:14.680 --> 01:38:16.974
The film's negative
is going to be up there.

1274
01:38:17.058 --> 01:38:18.351
And that's our real prize.

1275
01:38:18.434 --> 01:38:21.646
If these guards are alerted,
then I don't think we'll make it up.

1276
01:38:21.729 --> 01:38:23.773
It's vital that we control this lift.

1277
01:38:29.487 --> 01:38:32.824
This is called a parachute.

1278
01:38:33.324 --> 01:38:36.369
It means that one can jump
out of a plane safely.

1279
01:38:37.703 --> 01:38:38.704
So,

1280
01:38:39.497 --> 01:38:41.999
tomorrow at dawn I'll fly
the plane over the mountain

1281
01:38:42.083 --> 01:38:43.584
and Shola will jump out.

1282
01:38:44.252 --> 01:38:46.129
You land with the parachute,

1283
01:38:46.212 --> 01:38:50.842
take control of the lift,
and then you fire this flare.

1284
01:38:51.342 --> 01:38:52.718
It's a signal to me,

1285
01:38:52.802 --> 01:38:54.804
by which time
I'll have landed the plane,

1286
01:38:54.887 --> 01:38:57.014
made my way over
to the bottom of the lift,

1287
01:38:57.098 --> 01:38:58.599
while Polly provides cover.

1288
01:38:59.517 --> 01:39:02.520
Sir, I could do anything for you,

1289
01:39:02.603 --> 01:39:05.022
but I cannot jump out of an airplane.

1290
01:39:05.523 --> 01:39:07.316
And it's not that I wouldn't try,

1291
01:39:08.568 --> 01:39:10.695
it's that I know I'd let you down.

1292
01:39:11.612 --> 01:39:14.198
Yes. Well, I appreciate
your fear of heights,

1293
01:39:14.282 --> 01:39:17.743
but I am the only one who can fly.
So...

1294
01:39:17.827 --> 01:39:19.537
But you wouldn't have to land the plane.

1295
01:39:19.620 --> 01:39:21.914
You just have to land yourself.

1296
01:39:23.666 --> 01:39:26.085
Hmm. Well, it, um...

1297
01:39:27.128 --> 01:39:29.714
It would be bad form to ask
a man to do something

1298
01:39:29.797 --> 01:39:32.133
that I wouldn't do myself.

1299
01:39:32.216 --> 01:39:36.053
All right, Shola,
get ready for my signal.

1300
01:39:37.513 --> 01:39:38.848
We go at dawn.

1301
01:41:22.535 --> 01:41:24.120
Whoa.

1302
01:41:58.195 --> 01:41:59.280
Oh...

1303
01:43:41.799 --> 01:43:42.800
Shit!

1304
01:43:57.565 --> 01:43:58.941
- Oh!

1305
01:44:19.295 --> 01:44:22.798
Shh. That's it. That's it.

1306
01:44:34.185 --> 01:44:36.312
Answer the question, Dupont.

1307
01:44:36.395 --> 01:44:39.523
Do you know where Mata is?

1308
01:44:39.607 --> 01:44:40.608
No. I...

1309
01:44:40.691 --> 01:44:42.735
Well, you fuckin' should.

1310
01:44:42.818 --> 01:44:45.237
Because I sent her
to the American Embassy,

1311
01:44:45.321 --> 01:44:47.865
and she hasn't been seen since!

1312
01:44:49.366 --> 01:44:50.993
Do you see this?

1313
01:44:51.076 --> 01:44:54.663
If the American president
thinks he can fuck me too,

1314
01:44:54.747 --> 01:44:56.665
he is very much mistaken.

1315
01:44:56.749 --> 01:44:59.168
Take this negative to the press,

1316
01:44:59.251 --> 01:45:01.670
and it will ruin his reputation.

1317
01:45:01.754 --> 01:45:05.508
War will be the last thing
on the Americans' mind.

1318
01:45:05.591 --> 01:45:07.426
And when the scandal is over,

1319
01:45:07.510 --> 01:45:10.805
make sure the new president
is in our pocket!

1320
01:45:10.888 --> 01:45:12.973
Go on. Run! Run!

1321
01:45:13.057 --> 01:45:15.309
All the way to the White House.

1322
01:45:21.023 --> 01:45:22.316
Let's check the other side.

1323
01:45:22.399 --> 01:45:24.109
Let's go around to the south.

1324
01:45:26.654 --> 01:45:28.823
Make it snappy, pal!

1325
01:45:35.663 --> 01:45:36.664
Hey!

1326
01:45:43.295 --> 01:45:45.297
What the hell?

1327
01:45:52.346 --> 01:45:53.764
Buddy, what's the holdup?

1328
01:46:02.189 --> 01:46:03.232
Look!

1329
01:46:04.024 --> 01:46:05.276
There's the signal.

1330
01:46:05.359 --> 01:46:07.736
Get to the lift. I'll cover you.

1331
01:46:21.000 --> 01:46:22.042
Up on the hill!

1332
01:47:23.562 --> 01:47:25.981
Who the hell is that guy?

1333
01:47:46.543 --> 01:47:50.673
Shola! Stop fuckin' about!
Get on that counterweight!

1334
01:48:05.354 --> 01:48:07.064
Oh, fuck!

1335
01:48:07.648 --> 01:48:08.649
Oh...

1336
01:48:35.092 --> 01:48:37.469
Thank God you're here.

1337
01:48:38.595 --> 01:48:41.390
This plan hasn't exactly gone
by the numbers.

1338
01:48:47.730 --> 01:48:49.565
Polly. Do you have the film?

1339
01:48:49.648 --> 01:48:51.734
I have the negative
in my hand, Your Grace.

1340
01:48:52.401 --> 01:48:53.652
Well done.

1341
01:48:53.736 --> 01:48:55.571
So we have what we came for.

1342
01:48:55.654 --> 01:48:58.407
Yes. But the cause of all this mayhem
is still in there.

1343
01:48:59.283 --> 01:49:01.910
Enough of dealing with tentacles, Shola.

1344
01:49:01.994 --> 01:49:03.662
It's time to cut off the head.

1345
01:49:04.580 --> 01:49:06.290
It's good to have you back, sir.

1346
01:50:01.678 --> 01:50:06.183
You have got to be
fucking kidding me.

1347
01:50:06.266 --> 01:50:08.519
The thorn in my side

1348
01:50:08.602 --> 01:50:12.356
has just been
a peace-loving English rose.

1349
01:50:13.065 --> 01:50:17.111
The Duke of Oxford.
Good day to you, sir!

1350
01:50:17.986 --> 01:50:19.696
You are the very symbol

1351
01:50:19.780 --> 01:50:22.241
of everything I'm tryin' to destroy.

1352
01:50:22.324 --> 01:50:24.034
Aristocrats like you

1353
01:50:24.118 --> 01:50:27.371
stole my parents' mill
in Scotland when I was a lad.

1354
01:50:27.913 --> 01:50:31.583
Entitlement has "title" in it
for a reason, no? Huh!

1355
01:50:32.918 --> 01:50:36.171
I'm gonna fucking love killing you.

1356
01:50:36.255 --> 01:50:38.966
Come to papa, you posh prick!

1357
01:50:49.977 --> 01:50:50.977
I'm out.

1358
01:51:07.786 --> 01:51:10.664
The sound of silence.

1359
01:51:11.248 --> 01:51:14.751
It's my understanding that you, Duke,

1360
01:51:14.835 --> 01:51:16.879
are a formidable swordsman.

1361
01:51:17.713 --> 01:51:22.968
What say we end this shite as gentlemen?

1362
01:51:23.886 --> 01:51:25.053
After all,

1363
01:51:25.679 --> 01:51:28.098
manners maketh man.

1364
01:51:28.765 --> 01:51:31.935
A gentleman does not hide
in the shadows.

1365
01:51:33.187 --> 01:51:34.188
Aye.

1366
01:51:47.117 --> 01:51:48.744
Surprise.

1367
01:51:57.044 --> 01:51:58.170
Morton.

1368
01:51:59.880 --> 01:52:00.881
You see,

1369
01:52:01.632 --> 01:52:02.716
a little misplaced trust

1370
01:52:02.799 --> 01:52:04.927
allows one to get away with murder.

1371
01:52:05.010 --> 01:52:08.138
This debate should happen
after we have won the war.

1372
01:52:09.223 --> 01:52:13.060
I suggest we go to Russia,
and we sort it out ourselves.

1373
01:52:13.143 --> 01:52:14.853
And in poor Kitchener's case,

1374
01:52:17.439 --> 01:52:18.899
quite literally.

1375
01:52:22.694 --> 01:52:24.112
Spoken like a true traitor.

1376
01:52:24.196 --> 01:52:27.115
As far as I'm concerned, his blood...

1377
01:52:30.244 --> 01:52:32.454
that's on your grubby hands.

1378
01:52:35.082 --> 01:52:36.166
Two on one?

1379
01:52:37.084 --> 01:52:39.878
Behaving like a true gentleman.

1380
01:52:44.091 --> 01:52:45.676
You're delusional.

1381
01:52:46.343 --> 01:52:47.552
And you've killed millions.

1382
01:52:49.096 --> 01:52:51.848
What say one more, for good measure?

1383
01:52:52.683 --> 01:52:53.892
Hey!

1384
01:53:30.137 --> 01:53:32.306
Come on, old man.

1385
01:53:32.389 --> 01:53:34.016
- Get up.

1386
01:53:34.808 --> 01:53:36.893
I said, get up!

1387
01:54:58.266 --> 01:55:00.852
Fuck this gentleman shite.

1388
01:55:24.960 --> 01:55:26.294
Fuck's sake.

1389
01:55:33.427 --> 01:55:35.303
You bastard.

1390
01:56:12.090 --> 01:56:15.927
Give my regards to dear old Kitch, yeah?

1391
01:56:34.529 --> 01:56:37.491
You can't do it. You can't let me fall.

1392
01:56:37.574 --> 01:56:39.868
It goes against your every belief.

1393
01:56:39.951 --> 01:56:42.370
You are a pacifist.

1394
01:56:43.330 --> 01:56:45.832
And I'm now completely reliant

1395
01:56:45.916 --> 01:56:47.417
on your mercy, old boy.

1396
01:56:47.501 --> 01:56:50.545
You're right. I shouldn't let you fall.

1397
01:56:51.379 --> 01:56:56.468
Only now I have become the man
that my son would have been.

1398
01:56:59.513 --> 01:57:01.723
You...

1399
01:57:30.210 --> 01:57:31.503
Sir.

1400
01:57:31.586 --> 01:57:33.463
Shola, are you all right?

1401
01:57:34.464 --> 01:57:36.591
We've been through worse, Your Grace.

1402
01:57:38.009 --> 01:57:40.762
So, you'd jump
in front of a bullet for me,

1403
01:57:40.845 --> 01:57:42.597
but not out of an airplane?

1404
01:57:44.224 --> 01:57:45.809
So it would seem.

1405
01:57:47.143 --> 01:57:48.603
Thank you, my friend.

1406
01:57:48.687 --> 01:57:50.146
My pleasure.

1407
01:57:51.898 --> 01:57:53.608
- So, Shola.
- Hmm?

1408
01:57:53.692 --> 01:57:56.611
How are we going to get down from here?

1409
01:58:09.249 --> 01:58:10.667
Come in.

1410
01:58:11.334 --> 01:58:14.671
Mr. President, Chef has made
your favorite peanut butter cookies.

1411
01:58:19.926 --> 01:58:21.261
Thank you.

1412
01:58:37.444 --> 01:58:38.653
Oh...

1413
01:58:38.737 --> 01:58:42.073
Get me the generals, immediately.

1414
01:58:46.411 --> 01:58:48.663
We're goin' to war!

1415
01:59:04.763 --> 01:59:08.433
This victory is all down to you

1416
01:59:08.516 --> 01:59:11.811
and your fine son, Conrad.

1417
01:59:11.895 --> 01:59:15.065
And the courage of so many others, sir.

1418
01:59:15.148 --> 01:59:16.483
Of course.

1419
01:59:18.109 --> 01:59:20.820
Britain thanks you. And I thank you

1420
01:59:20.904 --> 01:59:23.365
for ensuring that
I didn't meet the same fate

1421
01:59:23.448 --> 01:59:24.658
as my cousins.

1422
01:59:25.742 --> 01:59:28.495
Wilhelm's abdication was understandable,

1423
01:59:29.746 --> 01:59:31.748
but what happened to Nicholas...

1424
01:59:34.626 --> 01:59:36.169
was despicable.

1425
01:59:36.252 --> 01:59:37.962
It was, sir.

1426
01:59:38.046 --> 01:59:39.839
I owe you a great personal debt

1427
01:59:39.923 --> 01:59:41.883
that I still have my crown.

1428
01:59:44.511 --> 01:59:46.012
In that case,

1429
01:59:46.096 --> 01:59:49.766
would you meet me tomorrow
at Kingsman, 3:00?

1430
01:59:49.849 --> 01:59:51.893
- A tailor shop?
- Yes, sir.

1431
01:59:51.976 --> 01:59:54.729
Number 11, Savile Row.

1432
01:59:59.984 --> 02:00:03.238
All of us here today are united,

1433
02:00:03.321 --> 02:00:07.117
sadly, in losing our sons and friends

1434
02:00:07.200 --> 02:00:09.244
in this terrible war.

1435
02:00:09.327 --> 02:00:12.163
What happened to this
generation of young men

1436
02:00:12.247 --> 02:00:14.332
must never happen again.

1437
02:00:14.416 --> 02:00:17.711
I believe the terms
of Versailles are too onerous,

1438
02:00:17.794 --> 02:00:22.215
too extreme, and could
precipitate another war.

1439
02:00:22.298 --> 02:00:25.051
What the world needs is an organization

1440
02:00:25.135 --> 02:00:26.428
that can channel its resources

1441
02:00:26.511 --> 02:00:31.057
towards preserving peace
and protecting life.

1442
02:00:31.141 --> 02:00:34.060
An independent intelligence agency

1443
02:00:34.144 --> 02:00:37.230
operating at the highest level
of discretion,

1444
02:00:37.313 --> 02:00:39.566
above the politics and bureaucracy

1445
02:00:39.649 --> 02:00:42.694
of government-run spy organizations.

1446
02:00:43.445 --> 02:00:44.696
To that end,

1447
02:00:45.530 --> 02:00:48.491
I have acquired this shop.

1448
02:00:48.575 --> 02:00:53.580
And I propose that we become
the founding members of

1449
02:00:54.289 --> 02:00:56.958
the Kingsman agency.

1450
02:00:58.626 --> 02:01:00.545
My code name will be...

1451
02:01:02.297 --> 02:01:03.423
Arthur.

1452
02:01:03.965 --> 02:01:05.383
And if you agree to join me,

1453
02:01:05.467 --> 02:01:07.051
you may turn over your place card,

1454
02:01:07.135 --> 02:01:09.554
where you will find your own code name.

1455
02:01:12.348 --> 02:01:14.350
I am Galahad.

1456
02:01:18.480 --> 02:01:19.898
I am Lancelot.

1457
02:01:21.566 --> 02:01:24.360
I am Bedivere.

1458
02:01:27.655 --> 02:01:29.574
I am Percival.

1459
02:01:29.657 --> 02:01:30.825
Excellent.

1460
02:01:32.160 --> 02:01:35.330
And this is Merlin,

1461
02:01:35.413 --> 02:01:38.333
who will be our quartermaster.

1462
02:01:39.292 --> 02:01:42.629
May our sons and friends rest in peace.

1463
02:01:42.712 --> 02:01:46.257
And long live the Kingsman.

1464
02:01:47.592 --> 02:01:49.427
The Kingsman.

1465
02:02:10.907 --> 02:02:12.784
Your body

1466
02:02:12.867 --> 02:02:16.621
Moves like a river
through a house of stone

1467
02:02:17.580 --> 02:02:19.290
So softly

1468
02:02:19.374 --> 02:02:22.919
Like a shadow never comes undone

1469
02:02:24.379 --> 02:02:26.673
You can never know

1470
02:02:26.756 --> 02:02:30.468
Your destiny

1471
02:02:30.552 --> 02:02:33.388
Or what the mirror shows you

1472
02:02:33.471 --> 02:02:37.225
Isn't real

1473
02:02:37.308 --> 02:02:40.395
Only you can

1474
02:02:40.478 --> 02:02:43.356
Truly understand

1475
02:02:43.439 --> 02:02:47.694
The measure of a hero

1476
02:02:47.777 --> 02:02:53.449
Is the measure of a man

1477
02:02:54.617 --> 02:03:01.082
The measure of a man

1478
02:03:02.292 --> 02:03:04.002
Nobody

1479
02:03:04.085 --> 02:03:07.714
Sees the man behind the face you show

1480
02:03:08.715 --> 02:03:10.466
Nobody

1481
02:03:10.550 --> 02:03:14.053
Feels the burden that is yours alone

1482
02:03:15.555 --> 02:03:17.724
You can never know

1483
02:03:17.807 --> 02:03:21.561
Your destiny

1484
02:03:22.061 --> 02:03:24.689
Or what the mirror shows you

1485
02:03:24.772 --> 02:03:28.526
Isn't real

1486
02:03:28.610 --> 02:03:31.738
Only you can

1487
02:03:31.821 --> 02:03:34.866
Truly understand

1488
02:03:34.949 --> 02:03:39.579
The measure of a hero

1489
02:03:39.662 --> 02:03:46.169
Is the measure of a man

1490
02:03:47.712 --> 02:03:50.715
Now it's time to address
the balance of my new flock.

1491
02:03:50.798 --> 02:03:53.426
Thanks to you, Comrade,
our left hand is strong.

1492
02:03:53.509 --> 02:03:54.761
But as you once said,

1493
02:03:54.844 --> 02:03:56.846
our right hand now needs strengthening.

1494
02:03:58.348 --> 02:03:59.933
Come in.

1495
02:04:04.812 --> 02:04:06.314
Don't be shy.

1496
02:04:06.898 --> 02:04:07.941
Come, come.

1497
02:04:12.403 --> 02:04:13.404
My Shepherd.

1498
02:04:14.113 --> 02:04:16.199
This young man will come to rival

1499
02:04:16.282 --> 02:04:18.618
your position in this world, my friend.

1500
02:04:19.702 --> 02:04:21.829
It is an honor, Comrade Lenin.

1501
02:04:23.915 --> 02:04:25.541
And your name?

1502
02:04:27.335 --> 02:04:29.045
Adolf Hitler.
